          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Records: Failure Modes, Key Measurements, and Maintenance Actions\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 1,898 operational records spanning ten asset classes (compressors, pumps, valves, heat exchangers, condensers, pipelines, reactors, separators, scrubbers, and turbines) across 399 stations. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (80\u2013899 kPa), temperature (\u221220 to 179 \u00b0C), flow (5\u2013899 m\u00b3/h), vibration (0.1\u20138.9 mm/s), and efficiency (70\u201398 percent). The analysis below identifies dominant failure modes, the measurements that discriminate healthy from degraded equipment, and concrete maintenance actions. Because the dataset is large, findings are presented by asset class, with cross-cutting themes addressed at the end.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Methodology and Screening Thresholds\n\nBefore classifying failures, consistent screening thresholds were applied across all records. These are drawn from standard rotating-equipment and pressure-system practice (ISO 10816 vibration zones, typical hydraulic efficiency bands, and process-envelope logic):\n\n| Parameter | Healthy | Watch | Alarm / Action Required |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Vibration | < 4.",
