          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Equipment Records: Failure Mode Assessment and Maintenance Prioritization\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 1,898 equipment records spanning ten asset classes (valves, pumps, compressors, turbines, condensers, heat exchangers, separators, scrubbers, reactors, and pipelines) across 399 stations. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration (mm/s), and efficiency (%). The analysis identifies anomalous operating signatures, infers likely failure modes, and recommends prioritized maintenance actions.\n\n**Key findings:**\n- 47 records exhibit vibration \u2265 8.5 mm/s, exceeding typical ISO 10816 Zone C/D boundaries and warranting corrective action.\n- 23 records show flow below 50 m\u00b3/h, indicating severe flow restriction, recirculation, or near-shutdown operation.\n- 14 records combine low flow with high vibration \u2014 the highest-risk signature in the dataset.\n- 6 records combine low flow with high pressure, suggesting blockage downstream or control valve malfunction.\n- Sub-zero temperature readings (down to \u221220 \u00b0C) on units expected to operate hot suggest either cryogenic service, sensor faults, or loss",
